THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

The FLAC encoder and decoder were written for flapus from the FLAC specification
(RFC 9639); they contain no code from libFLAC. The apodization window shapes and the
coefficient quantization follow libFLAC's documented behaviour (BSD, Copyright
Xiph.Org Foundation and Josh Coalson). FLAC is free of patents.

The Opus encoder is libopus 1.6.1 itself, generated from its sources by
tools/gen_opus_enc.py. The rest of the Opus part is a reimplementation of the Opus
reference software, with algorithms and tables derived from the projects below.
Their copyright notices and licenses follow, as they require.

